WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.649
You learned Gate 2's decisions: one
writer per attribute, one approver system

3
00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:10.575
per authority class, and a lane and
change-record type for each operation class.

4
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:15.650
You checked two provisioning configurations
for attributes with two writers,

5
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.187
and read each Finding, Warn and Info line.

6
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:21.113
And you saw why the alias
list and the directory

7
00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:23.663
name are inputs a reviewer has to confirm.

8
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:26.877
Before you ship, work through
the Chapter 08 checklist,

9
00:00:26.877 --> 00:00:31.163
and run the check whenever either
provisioning configuration changes.

10
00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:35.730
Next is Module 4, sources and the
starting drift: Gate 3 connects HR,

11
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.975
Entra ID and SailPoint on one key, and
you'll measure how far the directory is

12
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:46.440
from HR over two days, and compare the
runs without hiding what wasn't measured.
